+# Improve review — run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X
+
+- workflow: develop
+- branch integrated: this revisor pass (unmerged until approved)
+- status: succeeded (6.8 min, revisor pass — reason and cost in run detail)
+- generated: 2026-09-09 19:44+0000 by revisor `fabro_ask`
+
+---
+
+All six non-meta stages in this run (01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X, seed `fabro-c0e5`, PR #111) passed first-try — 6m23s wall, $0.371 total (planner $0.104 / implementer $0.213 / reviewer $0.054, from the run projection's stage billing). The recommendations below are the friction that actually showed up, ordered by expected impact.
+
+---
+
+**1. Keep the evidence capture inline — drop `current_seed_brief` from the reviewer's `preamble_allow_keys`** *(graph design / context engineering)*
+- **What happened:** The evidence capture was 13,998 bytes — under the reviewer node's `preamble_inline_max_kb=16` — yet it was still demoted to a blob ref because the aggregate 24 KB `preamble_budget_kb` was exceeded (capture + ~2.4 KB seed brief + ~2.5 KB `implementation_summary` + tester section, visible in the reviewer@1 prompt). The reviewer's very first action was a `read_file` of the blob at 14,295 bytes (worker log 19:36:37), and it then re-read parts via shell — while reporting *empty* `painpoints` even though its own prompt says "a workaround you performed is a painpoint" (reviewer journal, seq 288).
+- **Change:** In `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro` (reviewer node), remove `current_seed_brief` from `preamble_allow_keys` — the capture already embeds the authoritative seed spec — and/or raise `preamble_budget_kb` 24→32 (open seeds fabro-c1bb / fabro-8d2c). 
+- **Expected effect:** The capture renders inline; saves one tool round-trip + re-read on every review and removes the "unread blob ref" → `Verification blocked` failure class entirely.
+
+**2. The quality gate doesn't check the files this loop actually changes — add a loop-asset smoke tier** *(gate design / graph)*
+- **What happened:** The tester ran `just qualitygate` in 4.15s with output "no crates touched / format clean" (tester@1 output blob) — **zero machine verification** of the real changes (`evidence.nu`, `reviewer.md`). Verification fell entirely to LLM stages: the implementer hand-built a scratch-git exercise across many small turns (19:34–19:36), and the reviewer re-ran the exercise again (seq 288 journal: "re-ran the scratch-git exercise"). Those are the run's two costliest stages (216s + 58s inference).
+- **Change:** Add to the `qualitygate` recipe (justfile / `scripts/qualitygate.nu`): a `nu -c 'source ...'` parse check for `.fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/*.nu`, and check in the mixed-capture scratch exercise as `evidence-smoke.nu` following the existing `closeout-smoke.nu` pattern (the pattern exists in the same scripts dir — planner ls, seq 46). Note the regression test was **deleted** ("temp repo removed after run") because the brief mandated a cleaned-up scratch exercise.
+- **Expected effect:** Deterministic verification of loop-asset changes, durable regression coverage for the anomaly section, and fewer manual-verification LLM turns in the two most expensive stages.
+
+**3. A run that edits its own prompts reviews under the stale snapshot** *(engine / error handling)*
+- **What happened:** This seed's deliverable included a new adjudication line in `reviewer.md`, but the reviewer's injected prompt was the pre-change snapshot materialized at run creation. The reviewer noticed and verified the on-disk file instead (journal observation 3, seq 288) — benign here, but only because the reviewer happened to cross-check.
+- **Change:** Engine run-spec resolution: re-resolve prompt files (or at minimum append a "this run modified your prompt — judge the on-disk version, diff in evidence" notice) from the run branch tip at stage start — same mechanism open seed fabro-dc81 requests for `[run.pull_request]` in `lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/pipeline/publish.rs`.
+- **Expected effect:** Self-referential loop seeds (common in this repo — half the backlog targets prompts) can never silently review against superseded instructions.
+
+**4. Implementer re-fetches the seed it already has in full** *(prompting)*
+- **What happened:** The implementer prompt is internally contradictory: "## Input" says the brief "is authoritative — read it there FIRST; if the brief is thin, fetch the full seed", while step 1 mandates "Re-read the seed requirements from `sd show`". The implementer did both — `sd show fabro-c0e5` at seq 96 duplicated a 1.7 KB payload already fully present in its context.
+- **Change:** `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` step 1 → make the re-fetch conditional on brief quality (this is exactly open seed fabro-4881).
+- **Expected effect:** One fewer tool call + LLM turn per implementer pass (~5–10s and tokens on the stage that is 57% of run cost).
+
+**5. `sd ready --limit 200` is a firehose the planner doesn't need** *(tool usage)*
+- **What happened:** The planner's first call returned **200 seeds / 27,357 bytes** with `stdout_truncated: true` (seq 32); it only needed the top High-priority candidates (it picked #1). The tracker had ~22 High bugs and 160+ Medium/Low rows it paid to scan.
+- **Change:** PROJECT_FACTS sd table in `prompts/planner.md` (and planner.md step 1): use a top-N view (`--limit 10`) with fallback to the full list only when the top-N is exhausted — open seed fabro-c3b4.
+- **Expected effect:** Smaller first-turn context and less scan reasoning in every planner pass; eliminates the truncated-stdout ambiguity.
+
+**6. `ml record` flag contract cost a retry turn** *(error handling)*
+- **What happened:** The implementer's `ml record engine --type decision` failed with exit 1 — "decision records are missing required flag(s): --title, --rationale" (seq 182–186) — then retried successfully. The prompt's lesson-capture section demands the record but documents no per-type flag table (open seed fabro-96bd).
+- **Change:** Add the per-record-type flag table (`decision → --title --rationale`, etc.) to the implementer prompt's Lesson-capture section or PROJECT_FACTS.
+- **Expected effect:** Zero-retry lesson capture; also stops near-miss lessons from being silently skipped after a failed first attempt.
+
+**7. Stage progress denominator is wrong in every preamble** *(UX)*
+- **What happened:** The implementer's prompt said "Pipeline progress: 0 of 7 stages completed" (planner had completed); the reviewer's said "2 of 7" (four non-meta stages had completed). From the stage prompts at seq 86 and 250. Open seeds fabro-45bf / fabro-38f4.
+- **Change:** Engine preamble renderer — compute progress from unique completed nodes, not stage-section count.
+- **Expected effect:** Correct situational awareness in every downstream stage prompt and in the UI; removes a recurring "wrong data in context" wart.
+
+**8. Checkpoint snapshot+push on every boundary, including 300ms command nodes** *(engine efficiency)*
+- **What happened:** Each of the 6 stage boundaries ran a metadata snapshot (~1.7–2.3s) plus a git push (worker logs 19:36:13→15, 19:36:22→24, 19:36:26→29, 19:37:30→32, 19:37:35→38) — ~10–14s of a 6.4-minute run spent checkpointing stages that changed nothing but a journal line. Open seeds fabro-652d / fabro-c2ca.
+- **Change:** Batch checkpoint pushes at terminal/soft-exit boundaries; skip snapshots on non-agent command stages.
+- **Expected effect:** ~3–5% wall-time saving per run and fewer pushes; compounding across the ~30 runs/day this loop is doing.
+
+---
+
+One structural note tying #1 and #2 together: the run's cost profile (implementer 216s inference vs 3.7s tool time; reviewer 57s vs 0.4s) says this loop spends its budget on *LLM reasoning standing in for missing deterministic checks and detoured context* — the two highest-impact fixes are exactly the ones that move verification into the gate (#2) and deliver evidence without a detour (#1).
